    "program": "FAMILY + ACE LITTLE PROGRAM",
    "family": "NO FAM BEST FAM (We'll place you!)",
    "bio": "I feel like I've already written so much in this application, so I'm going to try and keep this part a little shorter. I grew up as a very quiet and reserved kid. I don't remember too much about my childhood except that all my friends were girls because I really didn't like guys (don't ask me why because even I don't know). I'd say my current life story really starts in high school, where I start going out with the \"it\" girl, as you could say, starting at the end of my freshman year of high school. Long story short, 2 years later she got blackout drunk, cheated on me, and now I still have to see her every week because we're both part of the leadership of a volunteer organization which is absolutely wonderful. I would say my life started after this break-up. Before the relationship even began, I was clinically depressed. I tried to take my own life through an overdose, but I didn't die. What I remember was waking up on the cold stone floor of my bathroom, and throwing up. I didn't die physically, but I felt like my old self died (yeah some real deep shit). So I tell my therapist about this, and I don't know what else I was expecting, but she sends me away to Willow Rock, which is a mental facility for potentially self endangering teenagers such as myself. We had nothing there, but our meals, other potentially dangerous people, and our beds, and for the first time, I started to really think. Okay, the details are kinda fuzzy, but flash forward to this period in my life where I'm actually full of hope and shit. I start writing about my feelings, I get really into philosophy, I get really into being present and being with nature and I discover Laufey (top 2 moments in my life). I was on a fucking roll. My confidence skyrockets, I love talking to people, I work harder than I ever have in my entire life. And for the first time in my life, I make friends, on my own. Pre-ex-girlfriend era, I was lowkey a loser and didn't associate with anyone. But now I had a group of guys who I'd stay out with until 5 in the morning when the sun started to rise. I had a group of girls that I could vent anything and everything to. It was like I realized wow maybe it's better to spread these things across multiple people instead of investing all my energy into one person i.e. girlfriend, and wow can you imagine how revelatory this information was for me at the time. Fast forward more, doing more thinking, more nature ing and hanging out ing, and I realize wow man you're freaking fat. I had gained 20 POUNDS like hot damn bro you're literally melting in it. My mental health is freefalling at this point because uhhh I lowkey stopped seeing a therapist because the one who put me in the psych ward made me hate all therapists but now I had no professional help. I am trying my best to hold it all together, but this getting fat shit really made me depressed again. And... oh em gee... guess who has a new boyfriend... that's right it's my ex-girlfriend (woohoo). So I am wallowing in self-hatred at this point. I'm really bad at telling my life story, so I'm going to skip to the modern day. Everyday, I wake up at 5 AM to commute to school. The first thing I do when I get there is go to the gym, and push every set to failure to feel the pain, because I am never going back to the way I was when I laid dying on that bathroom floor, begging God to make it all end. But life's pretty chill now, I'm still working on myself, trying to BE better, trying to build a future, and I hope that the start of college can be some new fresh slate for me. I try not to dwell to much on the past. I know what I want to make better to I make strides everyday. My life story is really not that interesting.",
    "interests": [
      "Music",
      "Concerts",
      "Reading"
    ],
    "hobbies": "- I love being outside in nature in general, but I especially love the beach, or hiking through forested areas and just exploring. - I love bird-watching, especially on shorelines or marshes, and specifically love bird photography. - I love to make and listen to music. I play the piano for a church choir and played cello for my high school's orchestra, and I've been trying to get into learning bass to get into a band. I've also just loved going to jazz clubs or classical concerts. - I've started getting into lifting and have been doing so for the last 2 months and I really enjoy pushing myself to the physical limit. - I enjoy reading and writing to some extent. I got really into philosophy and thought randomly and just like talking these things through my mind and trying to write them into words. - I got really randomly into gardening, though I haven't planted anything outside yet because winter is coming, but I'm making plans and learning things and want to grow things to put in my own food. - I enjoy thrifting and have been trying to get more into discovering my personal fashion. - I like to go outside and talk to random people if that makes sense. It's like people watching, but I just go up to them and talk to them until they either get uncomfortable or we just start talking. I just enjoy other people like generally not really sure if thats a hobby or activity.",
    "music": "I don't have favorite genres but I do have favorite artists: - Laufey: California & Me, Fragile, Dear Soulmate, Questions for The Universe, Carousel - Starfall: Cigarettes, Ink & Feather, Cruel, Feelings - Kali Uchis's entire new album - Bruno Mars's Silk Sonic album - Twice (randomly) - Rocco, d4vd (unfortunately), grentperez, - Chet Baker and Frank Sinatra if I'm feeling old - I'm into most music but it's very random but Laufey is absolutely number 1 (no clairo or beabadoobea because it's not performative but bea has some good songs like beaches and cruel affair that I mess with)",
    "movies": "Inside Out 2 broke me emotionally so now I cry no matter what movie I watch. I really liked Dexter, the serial killer, that I found through youtube shorts. The Green Mile was amazing.",
    "perfectDay": "I would wake up at 5 AM and drive all the way to Half-Moon Bay, specifically Seal Cove and watch the light emerge through the clouds, not really like watching the sunrise because it's way too overcast. Hopefully I'd see a heron, and the seals just chilling on the beach. I think around 7, I'd drive down into the Santa Cruz mountains, find a spot to picnic and think. For lunch, I'm eating a stale turkey and cheese sandwich with too much mayonaise. At this point in my life, I think I would just cry and sit there for a few hours afterward. Then, I'd drive a little farther down to Monterey to visit the aquarium, which I've always wanted to do but never got the chance to do. Hopefully on this perfect day, the Monterey Symphony Orchestra is performing Tchaikovsky's Romeo and Juliet Overture, and at 7PM, I would be in that concert hall listening to the greatest piece of classical music ever created. The concert would finish, and I would drive all the way back to this beach in Alameda that I don't remember the e of. I'd jump into the ocean, remembering how warm it was the last time I did, with all my clothes on. It's late by now, maybe 3 in the morning, so I'd drive home and pass out on my couch. I don't imagine doing all of this by myself, so I hope I'd have some friends along for the ride.",
