    "bio": "Hi, my e is Jida! I am the oldest of my family, with two younger brothers! I would define myself to be somewhat family-oriented, as I spend a lot of time with my family. A little about my academic background is that I'm a transfer student and a Psychology Major. I think that my journey as a transfer student was one of my most memorable experiences. Beginning college at my local CC, I was in a field that I wasn't entirely passionate about and that gave me a lot of self-doubt and hesitation. However, it also gave me time to reflect on myself and also give me the courage to make that change to switch majors. I chose psychology because for me, I've always found connecting to people super fulfilling! The mind is so expansive and of course, we are still learning about how humans behave and interact each and every day! My experience at SJSU has been both challenging and rewarding. Coming in as a transfer student, I didn't know many people. However, it gave me the opportunity to step out of my comfort zone and really have a fresh start. I've met so many people so far, either at club events or even my professors, who have enlightened me on their personal experiences at SJSU. SJSU has also pushed me to explore leadership opportunities and take the initiative to introduce myself to people; I'm honestly pleasantly surprised at myself and I don't think I wouldn't have done any of this otherwise. It's been a place where I've learned to take full advantage of the opportunities around me as of course, we always regret the chances we don't take! Overall, I hope to continue this path of self-growth in VSA and further challenge myself by taking on new responsibilities and giving back to my community!",
