    "bio": "In high school, I joined VSA my sophomore year of high school, I got accepted as a logistics intern and even though I didn’t get to do much, I was able to see the behind the scenes of how a cultural club functioned. I got to meet so many new people and dive deeper into my culture that I had felt so disconnected with. Although I grew up in an Asian household, I always felt more American than Asian and being in VSA helped me reconnect with who I am. The next year, my junior year I joined again and got accepted as a publicist. I got to put my creative skills to the test to make engaging Instagram posts. On top of being a publicist, I was involved in VSA’s fan dance, this was my second year on the team and I wanted to get more involved which is why I helped to choreograph one of the dances which we used in our annual cultural show. To get more involved with the club and to gain more leadership experience, I applied to be Vice President and I got accepted. Not only did I gain skills that will be useful outside of high school and into college, but I gained lifelong connections with people I will never forget. I hope joining VSA at SJSU will bring me a similar unforgettable experience like one I had in high school.",
