    "bio": "Hiii! My e is Michael Nguyen and I am a 2nd year here at SJSU. I am full viet and have lived in San Jose my whole life. I grew up having a sister (4 years younger) and have always looked out for her. Although we don't talk much, we always care for each other in silence which is cool in its way! During elementary I was a very outgoing kid, trying to make friends with everyone I saw and including everyone. I made lots and lots of friends but also realized as I grew up that I couldn't be friends with everybody. Some people I just didn't click with and at the time I was angry about it, but now as I look back, it was only natural! We never clicked and never got along with each other and thats how it goes. I was very close to all of my cousins as well, having weekly family reunions and bondings. I was a very chubby kid growing up and that kept going on for years. I was often bullied becuase of my weight and I grew up very insecure about how I looked. Entering middle school it was a huge jump and I started to ease down on my outgoing personality becuase everyone semeed so intimidating. This was when I met my core group of friends! I loved them and hung out with them every single day and they were by my side every day. I kept being made fun of becuase of how I looked and my weight and this would just anger me but my friends were there for me. Then quarantine hit. All of my cousins stopped talking to each other. My friends stopped talking to each other because they didn't own a computer. I only had a couple other friends. I only grew distant with all my friends and I didn't talk to anyone throughout this time. During this time, my escape from school and reality was video games and anime. I watched and played for hours on end until my eyes turned red and this cycle would just repeat. One day I just got tired of all the insults I'd face for how I looked and took control of my life. I started limiting the amount of time I'd spend in front of a screen and using that time to better my life (gym, eating healthy, etc..) By the time highschool came I was a whole different person. I was a healthier person overall but I become extremely introverted. I forgot how to talk to people as a whole. I soon reuinted with my middle school group and slowly started to open up again. I had to relearn how to socialize throughout my time in highschool. I was so focsued on chasing academics that I didn't take the time to build bonds during my time here. I graduated with the same group of friends I graduated with 4 years ago with this. My first year of university felt super boring as I never really got social with anyone, i just went to class and then went home. After finishing my first year of university I wanted to change that, that is why moving onto my 2nd year (current) I want to change and become more socialble. I want to be able to live a life worth remembering and a life full of fun memories!",
