    "family": "NO FAM BEST FAM (We'll place you!)",
    "bio": "Hii, I go by Phuong. I was born in Viet and moved to the US when I was 9 months old. My father had already lived in the US, while this was my mom’s first time being there. I was raised in San Jose and I still currently live here. The first time I went back to Viet was the summer after 6th grade. My family and I went on a vacation for around a month. First, I got to meet my mom’s side of the family in Nha Trang and we stayed with them for over a week. Then we went to see my dad’s family in Hanoi. I don’t have a lot of relatives in the US, so this was my first time meeting new family members. I was so surprised, I didn’t realize how many family members I actually had. I also got to see the cities and homes where my parents grew up. This experience allowed me to connect with my culture. This was really meaningful for me because I didn’t know much of my parents’ past. I also realized that they didn’t grow up as comfortably as I did, and it makes me feel more appreciative for what I have and the opportunities my parents never got.",
