    "family": "Red Phoenix",
    "bio": "My story has really been shaped by both the highs and the lows of college. On one hand, I’ve been lucky to find community through VSA and other orgs, stepping into leadership and mentorship roles that gave me a sense of purpose. I’ve grown a lot through those experiences, learning how much I enjoy guiding others and creating spaces where people feel supported and included. But on the other hand, I’ve also gone through some tough personal challenges, especially with friendships that didn’t end the way I thought they would. At one point, rumors and misunderstandings spread by people I was once close to made me feel isolated and questioned who I could trust. It was one of the hardest periods I’ve had to face, but it also pushed me to build resilience and figure out what values truly matter to me; honesty, accountability, and empathy. Through that, I’ve become someone who really values hearing people’s stories and making sure they feel understood. I don’t want anyone else to feel the way I did, unheard or misjudged, so I try to be the type of person who listens, supports, and helps others grow. At the same time, I’ve held onto the things that bring me joy, like traveling and exploring new places, or going to concerts and raves where I feel the freedom to just be myself. Those moments balance me out and remind me that life is about connection and experiences. Looking back, my story is about finding strength in challenges and learning to turn negative experiences into opportunities to grow and give back. That’s why being a Big is meaningful to me. I want to be a mentor who isn’t just there for advice, but also someone who shows up through both the struggles and the celebrations, and helps my Little feel like they have someone they can always count on.",
