    "bio": "Before I went to SJSU, I use to go to Ohlone community college. I would say I was a very different person compared to who I am today. During my cc days, I was less extroverted but I was always outside because I was going through a breakup. During that time I was always out and about especially at raves. When I came to SJSU, I felt that I was still the same outside person but now I would say I am more outgoing and love meeting people. I still go to raves but not as much as before. During my time in SJSU, I learned to grow how to be on my own, be less relient on my parents, and also be able to say that I can do it. At first I wasnt so sure that I would be able to make it on my own but when I recently went to Japan over the summer wihtout my parents was when I fully realized that I can get by on my own. While I was in Japan, I was able to learn how to put myself outside the box and be able to communicate with the people there and also understand that the difference in culture. Being in Japan helped me understand that theres more to life than just the life that I knew of in the Bay area.",
