    "bio": "TLDR: I didn't lock in my whole life, but I am locking tf in now. I was a perfectionist and everything I did or presented had to be perfect, otherwise I would rather not do it. I felt this way about my life too; if I was going to be average instead of excellent, I'd rather not be alive. I overcame my depression and that toxic mindset and now I just do things to the best of my ability. It's okay to be average; it's better to try and fall short than to never try and always wonder. In my undergrad, I just went to class, finished my assignments, and went home. I am returning for my MBA now, and I won't make the same mistakes again. I want to take advantage of as many events and opportunities possible. It's always more fun with more people, so I am always inviting those close to me. I also believe that a rising tide lifts all boats.",
